# 106-phase-1-demo.lua

The phase 1 demo program.  Run, not loaded:

    luajit src/phase-1-demo/106-phase-1-demo.lua [project folder]

(normally through `issues/completed/demos/phase-1-demo`, or
`run-phase-demo 1`).

What it does, in order:

1. Lists `input/` (each file's name, bytes, first line) — read first.  If
   `input/phase-1-demo.config` is there, its `key = value` lines are kept
   for step 3.
2. Loads the six phase 1 modules, reporting any that fail to load.
3. Gathers every options file; sets each config key to the first variant
   its builder listed, replaced by any value from
   `input/phase-1-demo.config` (see `105-demo-baseline.info.md`), and prints
   every key with where its value came from.
4. Runs each scene in `103-demo-sections.ORDER`: skipped with the reason if
   a needed module did not load; otherwise built, drawn and timed.  A scene
   that fails prints "COULD NOT RUN" with the error, and the rest go on.
5. Prints which scenes ran (with milliseconds) and which could not (why).
6. Writes `output/phase-1-demo.goodbye` (rewritten each run): run time, one
   line per scene, "N of M scenes ran.", "goodbye." — written last.

Scratch homes: `tmp/shared-memory/phase-1-demo/<scene>-<variant>/rao-home`.

Exit status: 0 when every scene ran, 1 otherwise.

No outward functions.
